-- חוק החוזים (חלק כללי), התשל"ג-1973 — sections 25, 26, 39 and 61: how a
-- contract is read, in both texts §25(א) has had (the one for a contract
-- made up to 6.1.2026, and amendment no. 3's for one made or renewed from
-- 7.1.2026); which of two readings §25(ב) and (ב1) prefer; what §25(ג)
-- and (ד) bring in; where §26 takes a detail the contract does not set;
-- §39's duty to perform in the customary way and in good faith; and what
-- §61 applies the law to. The text is laws/contracts-law.toml, pinned from
-- the live page of ספר החוקים הפתוח; the corpus holds no copy (MMS-529).
--
-- Why it is here: the corpus never cites the law, but every reading the
-- encoding takes of an agreement is a reading of a contract, and of a
-- circular or a takanon section a reading of a legal act that is not one.
-- Which text of §25(א) reads the corpus's instruments, and how §61(ב)
-- brings a circular under it, is the convention
-- reading.contracts-law, a pick for the lawyer.
--
-- §25(ב) and (ב1) each prefer one reading to another, and the law does not
-- say which wins where they pull apart (the reading that keeps the
-- contract is the drafter's). The two are two rules here, and neither is
-- weighed against the other.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties

§ `חוק החוזים (חלק כללי) — פירוש החוזה, השלמתו, תום לב ותחולה`

§§ `25`

-- The kinds of contract amendment no. 3's §25(א) tells apart.
@desc A contract, as the text of section 25(א) in force from 7.1.2026 tells kinds apart.
DECLARE `kind of contract under section 25` IS ONE OF
    `a business contract, as section 25 counts it`
    `a contract that is not a business contract, as section 25 counts it`
    `a standard contract, as section 25 counts it`
    `an employment contract or a collective agreement, as section 25 counts it`

@desc How section 25(א) reads a contract.
DECLARE `the way section 25 reads a contract` IS ONE OF
    `by the parties' intent, as it appears from the contract and the circumstances`
    `by its language, the parties' intent appearing explicitly from it`
    `by its language alone`
    `in the way the parties agreed it is read`

@desc What section 25(א) asks of a contract it reads.
DECLARE `contract section 25 reads` HAS
    `made or renewed on or after 7.1.2026` IS A BOOLEAN
    `its kind` IS A `kind of contract under section 25`
    `the parties agreed how it is read` IS A BOOLEAN @desc section 25(א)(1)
    `both parties had a lawyer in drafting it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc section 25(א)(5)(א): parties without one are counted as having agreed nothing on how it is read
    `its language alone gives a result that makes no sense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc section 25(א)(2)(א)
    `its language alone sets its provisions against each other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc section 25(א)(2)(ב)
    `the parties' intent appears explicitly from its language` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the earlier text's second limb

-- The earlier text, for a contract made up to 6.1.2026: by the parties'
-- intent as it appears from the contract and the circumstances; but where
-- that intent appears explicitly from the language, by the language.
@ref law:25
GIVEN c IS A `contract section 25 reads`
GIVETH A `the way section 25 reads a contract`
DECIDE `the way section 25's earlier text reads it` c IS
    IF c's `the parties' intent appears explicitly from its language`
    THEN `by its language, the parties' intent appearing explicitly from it`
    ELSE `by the parties' intent, as it appears from the contract and the circumstances`

-- (5)(א): parties no lawyer represented in drafting it are counted as
-- having agreed nothing on how it is read.
@ref law:25
GIVEN c IS A `contract section 25 reads`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the parties' agreement on reading it counts under section 25` c IF
        c's `the parties agreed how it is read`
    AND c's `both parties had a lawyer in drafting it`

-- (2)(א)-(ב) and (3): a contract to be read by its language alone, whose
-- language alone gives a result that makes no sense or sets its provisions
-- against each other, is read by the rest of the law, (4) among it.
@ref law:25
GIVEN c IS A `contract section 25 reads`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `its language alone fails under section 25` c IF
        c's `its language alone gives a result that makes no sense`
    OR  c's `its language alone sets its provisions against each other`

-- The text from 7.1.2026. (4): a contract that is not a business contract,
-- a standard contract even where it says otherwise, and an employment
-- contract or a collective agreement are read by the parties' intent, from
-- the contract and the circumstances. (1): otherwise the way the parties
-- agreed, where they did. (2): a business contract that sets no way is read
-- by its language alone, unless that language fails (3).
-- (1) also binds an employment contract or a collective agreement whose
-- parties agreed how it is read: (4) speaks of a contract the parties made
-- no such agreement for, and the words "אף אם הוסכם בו אחרת" attach to the
-- standard contract alone. An agreement on the way it is read stands until
-- that way is to read it by its language alone and the language fails;
-- then (3) sends it to (4).
@ref law:25
GIVEN c IS A `contract section 25 reads`
GIVETH A `the way section 25 reads a contract`
DECIDE `the way section 25's text from 7.1.2026 reads it` c IS
    CONSIDER c's `its kind`
    WHEN `a standard contract, as section 25 counts it`
        THEN `by the parties' intent, as it appears from the contract and the circumstances`
    WHEN `a business contract, as section 25 counts it`
        THEN IF `the parties' agreement on reading it counts under section 25` c
             THEN `in the way the parties agreed it is read`
             ELSE IF `its language alone fails under section 25` c
                  THEN `by the parties' intent, as it appears from the contract and the circumstances`
                  ELSE `by its language alone`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the parties' agreement on reading it counts under section 25` c
        THEN `in the way the parties agreed it is read`
        ELSE `by the parties' intent, as it appears from the contract and the circumstances`

@ref law:25
GIVEN c IS A `contract section 25 reads`
GIVETH A `the way section 25 reads a contract`
DECIDE `the way section 25 reads it` c IS
    IF c's `made or renewed on or after 7.1.2026`
    THEN `the way section 25's text from 7.1.2026 reads it` c
    ELSE `the way section 25's earlier text reads it` c

-- (ב) and (ב1): of two readings of a contract that bears both, the one
-- that keeps it in force is preferred to one by which it is void; and
-- where one party had the upper hand in shaping its terms, the reading
-- against that party is preferred to the reading in its favour. (5)(ב):
-- the parties' agreement against (ב1) has no effect.
@desc A reading of a contract that bears more than one, as section 25(ב) and (ב1) weigh it.
DECLARE `reading of a contract under section 25` HAS
    `keeps the contract in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `favours the party that had the upper hand in shaping its terms` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref law:25
GIVEN a IS A `reading of a contract under section 25`, b IS A `reading of a contract under section 25`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 25(ב) prefers the one reading to the other` a b IF
        a's `keeps the contract in force`
    AND NOT b's `keeps the contract in force`

@ref law:25
GIVEN a IS A `reading of a contract under section 25`, b IS A `reading of a contract under section 25`, `one party had the upper hand in shaping its terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 25(ב1) prefers the one reading to the other` a b `one party had the upper hand in shaping its terms` IF
        `one party had the upper hand in shaping its terms`
    AND NOT a's `favours the party that had the upper hand in shaping its terms`
    AND b's `favours the party that had the upper hand in shaping its terms`

-- (ג): an expression or a term used in contracts of the same kind carries
-- the meaning it is known to have in them.
@ref law:25
GIVEN `it is used in contracts of the same kind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 25(ג) reads it by its known meaning in such contracts` `it is used in contracts of the same kind` IS
    `it is used in contracts of the same kind`

-- (ד): sections 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 and 10 of the Interpretation Law, 1981,
-- and §57ג of the Evidence Ordinance, apply to reading a contract too,
-- where nothing else provides and nothing in the matter or its context is
-- inconsistent with it. The Interpretation Law is not encoded (MMS-689).
@ref law:25
`the Interpretation Law's sections section 25(ד) applies to a contract` MEANS
    LIST 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 10

@ref law:25
GIVEN `another provision governs the matter` IS A BOOLEAN, `the matter or its context is inconsistent with it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 25(ד) applies those sections` `another provision governs the matter` `the matter or its context is inconsistent with it` IF
        NOT `another provision governs the matter`
    AND NOT `the matter or its context is inconsistent with it`

§§ `26`

-- A detail the contract, or what it refers to, does not set is taken from
-- the practice between the parties; where there is none, from the practice
-- usual in contracts of that kind; and it is then counted as agreed.
@desc Where section 26 takes a detail the contract does not set.
DECLARE `where section 26 takes a missing detail` IS ONE OF
    `from the practice between the parties`
    `from the practice usual in contracts of that kind`
    `section 26 gives it no source`

@ref law:26
GIVEN `there is a practice between the parties` IS A BOOLEAN, `there is a practice usual in contracts of that kind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `where section 26 takes a missing detail`
DECIDE `the source section 26 gives a missing detail` `there is a practice between the parties` `there is a practice usual in contracts of that kind` IS
    IF `there is a practice between the parties`
    THEN `from the practice between the parties`
    ELSE IF `there is a practice usual in contracts of that kind`
         THEN `from the practice usual in contracts of that kind`
         ELSE `section 26 gives it no source`

§§ `39`

-- An obligation that arises from a contract is performed in the customary
-- way and in good faith, and so is a right that arises from one used.
-- The party is either side of an agreement or a teacher's contract.
@desc What section 39 of the Contracts Law asks of a party.
DECLARE `Contracts Law section 39 act` IS ONE OF
    `perform the obligation the contract gives in the customary way and in good faith`
    `use the right the contract gives in the customary way and in good faith`

@ref law:39
GIVEN p IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Contracts Law section 39 act`
DECIDE `performance in good faith under section 39` p IS
    PARTY p
    MUST  `perform the obligation the contract gives in the customary way and in good faith`
    LEST  BREACH BY p BECAUSE "Contracts Law, section 39: an obligation arising from a contract is performed in the customary way and in good faith"

@ref law:39
GIVEN p IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Contracts Law section 39 act`
DECIDE `use of a right in good faith under section 39` p IS
    PARTY p
    MUST  `use the right the contract gives in the customary way and in good faith`
    LEST  BREACH BY p BECAUSE "Contracts Law, section 39: a right arising from a contract is used in the customary way and in good faith"

§§ `61`

-- (א): the law applies where no other law provides specially for the
-- matter. (ב): so far as it suits the matter, and with the changes it
-- requires, to legal acts that are not a contract and to obligations that
-- do not arise from one.
@desc An instrument of the corpus, as the Contracts Law meets it.
DECLARE `instrument the Contracts Law meets` IS ONE OF
    `a contract: an agreement or a teacher's contract of employment`
    `a legal act that is not a contract: a circular, the takanon or a letter`

@desc How the Contracts Law reaches an instrument.
DECLARE `how the Contracts Law reaches it` IS ONE OF
    `as a contract`
    `under section 61(ב), so far as it suits the matter`
    `not: another law provides specially for the matter`

@ref law:61
GIVEN i IS AN `instrument the Contracts Law meets`, `another law provides specially for the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `how the Contracts Law reaches it`
DECIDE `how section 61 brings the Contracts Law to it` i `another law provides specially for the matter` IS
    IF `another law provides specially for the matter`
    THEN `not: another law provides specially for the matter`
    ELSE CONSIDER i
         WHEN `a contract: an agreement or a teacher's contract of employment` THEN `as a contract`
         WHEN `a legal act that is not a contract: a circular, the takanon or a letter` THEN `under section 61(ב), so far as it suits the matter`
